  "notes": "Yamamoto-first discovery pass under the current durable repository authority. docs/PRIORITIES.md, docs/EDITORIAL.md, docs/DOMAINS.md, and radar/inbox/README.md were reread before research or grading. Fresh checks of Tsuyoshi Yamamoto, Jazz House ALFIE, BODY&SOUL, current schedule traces, Space M&A, and credible Japanese-jazz sources found no additional verified unrecorded Yamamoto performance requiring a new RADAR record; already-canonical or already-curated dates were not duplicated. Stage 1 admits Tohji Last Live “TOKYO MALL” for a specific historical/live reason rather than fame or venue prestige: Tohji has announced the end of his music activity in 2026, this Tokyo Dome concert is explicitly billed as his final live performance, and the setting deliberately closes a long-running artistic thread because the Dome appears in Mall Boyz’s “Higher” and a new 'Higher 2026 in 東京ドーム' version was created around the farewell. Stage 2 assigns S only after an explicit scarcity challenge. The concrete non-repeatability is the announced final performance of his music career. A+ would understate the genuine-regret case created by a documented career endpoint; S+ would overstate the broader historical claim because current evidence supports a singular farewell for Tohji but does not establish an 'alter plans' event of wider historical exceptionalism. The current rubric was reread before finalizing this S, and the batch adds no S+ event. Batch distribution: A 0, A+ 0, S 1, S+ 0.",
