      "factual_description": "Tohji will present Tohji Last Live “TOKYO MALL” at Tokyo Dome on November 17, 2026. Spincoaster lists doors at 16:00, a concert start at 18:00 and a planned end at 20:30, with CANTEEN Inc. as planner/producer, and reports that Tohji has announced the end of his music activity in 2026 and that this will be his final live performance. Spincoaster also notes that he has remained independent rather than joining a major label and that Tokyo Dome appears in the lyrics of Mall Boyz’s “Higher.” LiFTED Japan documents the newly recorded 'Higher 2026 in 東京ドーム' video, which combines the original video with footage shot inside Tokyo Dome and makes that earlier lyric literal ahead of the farewell. The official concert site lists face-value reserved seating at ¥14,800 and reserved seating with a T-shirt at ¥19,800. Its fastest presale application window ran August 9–23, 2026.",
